---
# 13 Analisis Modal - Porticos Espaciales
---
@{config align:left}

## Ejemplo 13.1 - Portico Espacial (Paz & Kim, 6th Ed.)

@{text}
Este ejemplo muestra el analisis modal de un portico espacial con 5 nodos
y 4 elementos. El nodo 1 (central, libre) esta conectado a los nodos 2-5
(fijos). Se utiliza la funcion SpaceFrameElement del MATLAB del libro
para calcular automaticamente la matriz de transformacion T usando un
tercer nodo de referencia y productos vectoriales (cross product).
@{end text}

@{awatif 700 450}
// Nodos escalados /100: 0=(0,0,0) libre, 1-4 fijos
node 0 0 0
node 0 0 -2
node 0 2 0
node -2 0 0
node 0 -2 0
// Elementos (nodo_inicio nodo_fin)
element frame 0 1 E:30e6 A:50 Iz:200 Iy:200
element frame 0 2 E:30e6 A:28 Iz:64 Iy:64
element frame 0 3 E:30e6 A:50 Iz:200 Iy:200
element frame 0 4 E:30e6 A:28 Iz:64 Iy:64
// Apoyos
support 1 fixed
support 2 fixed
support 3 fixed
support 4 fixed
@{end awatif}
> -Fig. 13.1- Portico espacial - Ejemplo 13.1 (Paz & Kim, 6th Ed.)

---
## 1. Propiedades del Material
@{cells} |E = 30000000|G = 12000000|
> E, G en psi

## 2. Propiedades de los Elementos (Table 13.1)
> Elementos 1 y 3: secciones grandes
@{cells} |A1 = 50|Iz1 = 200|Iy1 = 200|J1 = 40|
@{cells} |m1 = 0.2|I01 = 205|
> A (in^2), Iz,Iy,J,I0 (in^4), m (lb*s^2/in^2)

> Elementos 2 y 4: secciones pequenas
@{cells} |A2 = 28|Iz2 = 64|Iy2 = 64|J2 = 12.8|
@{cells} |m2 = 0.1|I02 = 68|

## 3. Geometria - Coordenadas de Nodos
> 5 nodos: 1=(0,0,0), 2=(0,0,-200), 3=(0,200,0), 4=(-200,0,0), 5=(0,-200,0)

nodes = [[0,0,0],[0,0,-200],[0,200,0],[-200,0,0],[0,-200,0]]

## 4. Conectividad (n1, n2, nref)
> Cada elemento tiene nodo inicial, final y un nodo de referencia para definir la orientacion
> conn = [1,2,3; 1,3,2; 1,4,2; 1,5,2]

conn = [[1,2,3],[1,3,2],[1,4,2],[1,5,2]]

---
## 5. Rigidez Local y Transformacion Automatica (SpaceFrameElement)

@{text}
La matriz de transformacion T se calcula automaticamente usando un tercer
nodo de referencia. El procedimiento es:
1. ex = (n2 - n1)/L (vector unitario a lo largo del elemento)
2. ey = cross(n3 - n1, n2 - n1) / |...| (perpendicular)
3. ez = cross(ex, ey) (tercer eje)
4. H = [ex; ey; ez] (3x3 rotation)
5. T = blkdiag(H, H, H, H) (12x12 transformation)
6. K_global = T' * K_local * T
@{end text}

> Propiedades por elemento
n_e = 4
A_el = [[A1],[A2],[A1],[A2]]
Iz_el = [[Iz1],[Iz2],[Iz1],[Iz2]]
Iy_el = [[Iy1],[Iy2],[Iy1],[Iy2]]
J_el = [[J1],[J2],[J1],[J2]]
mbar_el = [[m1],[m2],[m1],[m2]]
I0_el = [[I01],[I02],[I01],[I02]]

> Matrices de rigidez global y masa global (ensambladas)
> Solo nodo 1 es libre (6 DOFs: 1-6), nodos 2-5 fijos
> Cada elemento conecta nodo 1 con un nodo fijo
> Solo la submatriz [1:6, 1:6] de cada K_global contribuye

K_G = zeros(6, 6)
M_G = zeros(6, 6)

for el = 1:n_e
> --- Nodos del elemento ---
i1 = conn[el, 1]
i2 = conn[el, 2]
i3 = conn[el, 3]

x1 = nodes[i1, 1]
y1 = nodes[i1, 2]
z1 = nodes[i1, 3]
x2 = nodes[i2, 1]
y2 = nodes[i2, 2]
z2 = nodes[i2, 3]
x3 = nodes[i3, 1]
y3 = nodes[i3, 2]
z3 = nodes[i3, 3]

> --- Longitud ---
dx = x2 - x1
dy = y2 - y1
dz = z2 - z1
Le = sqrt(dx^2 + dy^2 + dz^2)

> --- Vector unitario ex (n2-n1)/L ---
exx = dx/Le
exy = dy/Le
exz = dz/Le

> --- Vector n3-n1 ---
v31x = x3 - x1
v31y = y3 - y1
v31z = z3 - z1

> --- Vector n2-n1 ---
v21x = dx
v21y = dy
v21z = dz

> --- ey = cross(n3-n1, n2-n1) normalizado ---
cyx = v31y*v21z - v31z*v21y
cyy = v31z*v21x - v31x*v21z
cyz = v31x*v21y - v31y*v21x
cym = sqrt(cyx^2 + cyy^2 + cyz^2)
eyx = cyx/cym
eyy_v = cyy/cym
eyz = cyz/cym

> --- ez = cross(ex, ey) ---
ezx = exy*eyz - exz*eyy_v
ezy = exz*eyx - exx*eyz
ezz = exx*eyy_v - exy*eyx

> --- Matriz H (3x3) ---
H = [[exx,exy,exz],[eyx,eyy_v,eyz],[ezx,ezy,ezz]]

> --- T (12x12) = blkdiag(H,H,H,H) ---
T = zeros(12, 12)
for ii = 1:3
for jj = 1:3
T[ii, jj] = H[ii, jj]
T[ii+3, jj+3] = H[ii, jj]
T[ii+6, jj+6] = H[ii, jj]
T[ii+9, jj+9] = H[ii, jj]
end
end

> --- Propiedades del elemento ---
Ae = A_el[el, 1]
Ize = Iz_el[el, 1]
Iye = Iy_el[el, 1]
Je = J_el[el, 1]

EIz = E*Ize
EIy = E*Iye
GJ = G*Je
EA = E*Ae

> --- K local (12x12) - Eq 6.1 ---
k = [[EA/Le,0,0,0,0,0,-(EA/Le),0,0,0,0,0],[0,(12*EIz)/Le^3,0,0,0,(6*EIz)/Le^2,0,-((12*EIz)/Le^3),0,0,0,(6*EIz)/Le^2],[0,0,(12*EIy)/Le^3,0,-((6*EIy)/Le^2),0,0,0,-((12*EIy)/Le^3),0,-((6*EIy)/Le^2),0],[0,0,0,GJ/Le,0,0,0,0,0,-(GJ/Le),0,0],[0,0,-((6*EIy)/Le^2),0,(4*EIy)/Le,0,0,0,(6*EIy)/Le^2,0,(2*EIy)/Le,0],[0,(6*EIz)/Le^2,0,0,0,(4*EIz)/Le,0,-((6*EIz)/Le^2),0,0,0,(2*EIz)/Le],[-(EA/Le),0,0,0,0,0,EA/Le,0,0,0,0,0],[0,-((12*EIz)/Le^3),0,0,0,-((6*EIz)/Le^2),0,(12*EIz)/Le^3,0,0,0,-((6*EIz)/Le^2)],[0,0,-((12*EIy)/Le^3),0,(6*EIy)/Le^2,0,0,0,(12*EIy)/Le^3,0,(6*EIy)/Le^2,0],[0,0,0,-(GJ/Le),0,0,0,0,0,GJ/Le,0,0],[0,0,-((6*EIy)/Le^2),0,(2*EIy)/Le,0,0,0,(6*EIy)/Le^2,0,(4*EIy)/Le,0],[0,(6*EIz)/Le^2,0,0,0,(2*EIz)/Le,0,-((6*EIz)/Le^2),0,0,0,(4*EIz)/Le]]

> --- K global = T' * k * T ---
Kg = transpose(T)*k*T

> --- M local consistente (Eq 6.20) ---
mb = mbar_el[el, 1]
I0e = I0_el[el, 1]
r = I0e/Ae
fac = mb*Le/420

ml = [[140,0,0,0,0,0,70*r,0,0,0,0,0],[0,156,0,0,0,22*Le,0,54,0,0,0,-13*Le],[0,0,156,0,-22*Le,0,0,0,54,0,13*Le,0],[0,0,0,140*r,0,0,0,0,0,70*r,0,0],[0,0,-22*Le,0,4*Le^2,0,0,0,-13*Le,0,-3*Le^2,0],[0,22*Le,0,0,0,4*Le^2,0,13*Le,0,0,0,-3*Le^2],[70,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,0,0,0,0],[0,54,0,0,0,13*Le,0,156,0,0,0,-22*Le],[0,0,54,0,-13*Le,0,0,0,156,0,22*Le,0],[0,0,0,70*r,0,0,0,0,0,140*r,0,0],[0,0,13*Le,0,-3*Le^2,0,0,0,22*Le,0,4*Le^2,0],[0,-13*Le,0,0,0,-3*Le^2,0,-22*Le,0,0,0,4*Le^2]]

ml = fac*ml

> --- M global = T' * ml * T ---
Mg = transpose(T)*ml*T

> --- Ensamblar: nodo 1 es comun a todos los elementos ---
> Para nodo 1 (libre), usamos DOFs 1-6 del elemento (filas/cols 1:6 de Kg)
for i = 1:6
for j = 1:6
K_G[i, j] = K_G[i, j] + Kg[i, j]
M_G[i, j] = M_G[i, j] + Mg[i, j]
end
end
end

---
## 6. Matrices Ensambladas

> Rigidez global (6x6):
K_G

> Masa global (6x6):
M_G

---
## 7. Eigenvalores - Frecuencias Naturales
> Problema generalizado: K*phi = omega^2 * M * phi
> Equivalente: inv(M)*K*phi = omega^2 * phi

D = inv(M_G)*K_G
ev = eigenvalues(D)

> Frecuencias naturales (Hz)
omega1 = sqrt(ev.(1))
f1 = omega1/(2*pi)

omega2 = sqrt(ev.(2))
f2 = omega2/(2*pi)

omega3 = sqrt(ev.(3))
f3 = omega3/(2*pi)

omega4 = sqrt(ev.(4))
f4 = omega4/(2*pi)

omega5 = sqrt(ev.(5))
f5 = omega5/(2*pi)

omega6 = sqrt(ev.(6))
f6 = omega6/(2*pi)

---
## 8. Periodos Naturales
T1 = 1/f1
T2 = 1/f2
T3 = 1/f3
T4 = 1/f4
T5 = 1/f5
T6 = 1/f6

---
## 9. Resumen de Frecuencias

@{text}
Frecuencias naturales del portico espacial con masa consistente.
Solo el nodo 1 (central) es libre, con 6 DOFs (3 traslacionales + 3 rotacionales).
Los 4 nodos perifericos (2-5) estan empotrados.
@{end text}

> Frecuencias (Hz):
@{cells} |f_1 = f1|f_2 = f2|f_3 = f3|
@{cells} |f_4 = f4|f_5 = f5|f_6 = f6|
> Frecuencias en Hz
